---
description: Security baseline — always applied
alwaysApply: true
---

Security non-negotiables for any change:

- Never commit secrets. `.env` gitignored; `.env.example` committed with placeholders.
- All endpoints `[Authorize]` by default; `[AllowAnonymous]` only explicit.
- User identity from validated JWT claims, never from request body.
- Resource ownership checked on every mutation.
- Parameterized queries only. No string concatenation with user input.
- Frontend: tokens in memory + httpOnly refresh cookie. Never `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`.
- No `any` type in TypeScript. Use `unknown` and narrow.

Full detail: `.ai-kit/ai/conventions/security.md`.
